research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/cor-root-test-dominates-ratio-test.md-83-
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/cor-root-test-dominates-ratio-test.md-84-[L4] The root test: for a family from $1$, $\limsup_k |a_{k+1}|^{1/(k+1)} < 1$ gives convergence of $\sum_{k \ge 1}|a_k|$ and hence of $\sum_{k \ge 1} a_k$, and $> 1$ gives divergence of $\sum_{k \ge 1} a_k$ ([[thm-root-test]]).
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/cor-root-test-dominates-ratio-test.md-85-
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/cor-root-test-dominates-ratio-test.md:86:[L5] The ratio test: $\limsup_k q_k < 1$ gives convergence of $\sum |a_k|$ and hence of $\sum a_k$, and $\liminf_k q_k > 1$ gives divergence of $\sum a_k$ ([[thm-ratio-test]]).
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/cor-root-test-dominates-ratio-test.md-87-
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/cor-root-test-dominates-ratio-test.md-88-[L6] A series converges if and only if each of its tail series converges ([[lem-series-tail-invariance]], [[def-series]]).
