research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-448293-+          "quote": "The hypothesis $a_k \\ne 0$ is what makes $q_k$ exist and is not a convenience: a\nsingle vanishing term leaves the ratio at that index undefined. For a family from\na starting index $m$ the statement is the one above applied to the shifted\nsequence $j \\mapsto a_{j+m}$ ([[def-series]]), whose ratios are\n$|a_{j+m+1}/a_{j+m}|$.",
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-448294-+          "uses": [
--
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-449907-+        },
