research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-470997-1.1 Fix $j \in \mathbb{N}$ and put $n := j + N$, so that $N \le n$ and $n - N = j$. [given]
--
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-471128-5.2 In the case $\rho > 1$: the sequence $j \mapsto a_{j+1}$ does not converge to $0$, because with the rational tolerance $1$ no index $K$ satisfies $|a_{k+1}| < 1$ for all $k \ge K$; hence $\sum_{k \ge 1} a_k$ diverges, which is claim 2. [step 4.2, L7]
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-471129-6.1 In the case $\rho < 1$: the series $\sum_{k \ge 1} |a_k|$ having been shown to converge, the sequence $j \mapsto a_{j+1}$ has a convergent absolute-value series, so $\sum_{k \ge 1} a_k$ converges as well; together with the convergence of $\sum_{k \ge 1}|a_k|$ that is claim 1. [step 5.1, L11]
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-471130-7.1 The three cases $\rho < 1$, $\rho > 1$ and $\rho = 1$ exhaust $\overline{\mathbb{R}}$, the extended order being total, so the three claims together cover every family. [step 6.1, step 5.2, step 3.3, L1, cases-exhaustive] ∎
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:471131:## thm-ratio-test
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-471132-1.1 Assume $\limsup_{k} q_k < 1$. [assume-case lt]
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-471133-1.2 Assume instead $\liminf_{k} q_k > 1$. [assume-case gt]
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-471134-1.3 Each $q_k$ is a nonnegative real, being a quotient of a nonnegative real by a positive one, so every $s_n \ge q_n \ge 0$ and hence $\limsup_k q_k \ge 0$. [given, L1, L3]
--
