items/cor-rational-root-of-an-integer-is-an-integer.md-2-id: cor-rational-root-of-an-integer-is-an-integer
items/cor-rational-root-of-an-integer-is-an-integer.md-3-kind: corollary
items/cor-rational-root-of-an-integer-is-an-integer.md:4:title: "A rational root of $x^{k} = m$ is an integer: if $k \\ge 1$, $m \\in \\mathbb{Z}$, $x \\in \\mathbb{Q}$ and $x^{k}$ is the image of $m$, then $x$ is the image of an integer"
items/cor-rational-root-of-an-integer-is-an-integer.md-5-status: published
items/cor-rational-root-of-an-integer-is-an-integer.md-6-origin: session
items/cor-rational-root-of-an-integer-is-an-integer.md-7-provenance:
--
items/cor-rational-root-of-an-integer-is-an-integer.md-95-
items/cor-rational-root-of-an-integer-is-an-integer.md-96-1.3 Suppose first $x = 0$. Since $k \ge 1$, write $k = \sigma(t)$; then $x^{k} = x^{t} \cdot 0 = 0 = j(0)$, so $j(m) = j(0)$ and $m = 0$ by injectivity of $j$; and $x = 0 = j(0)$ is the image of an integer. [L3, L4, L5, L12]
items/cor-rational-root-of-an-integer-is-an-integer.md-97-
items/cor-rational-root-of-an-integer-is-an-integer.md:98:1.4 Suppose instead $x \ne 0$, and write $x = [(a,b)]$ with $b \ne 0$; then $a \ne 0$. If $b < 0$, replace $(a,b)$ by $(-a,-b)$, which represents the same rational because $a(-b) = (-a)b$; so we may assume $b > 0$. [L1, L2, L13, choose]
items/cor-rational-root-of-an-integer-is-an-integer.md-99-
items/cor-rational-root-of-an-integer-is-an-integer.md-100-2.1 For a prime $q$, an integer $u$ and $t \ge 1$: if $q \mid u^{t}$ then $q \mid u$. Let $S$ be the set of $t$ for which this implication holds; $0 \in S$ vacuously, since $t \ge 1$ fails there. Suppose $t \in S$ and $q \mid u^{\sigma(t)} = u^{t} u$. By [L9] either $q \mid u^{t}$ or $q \mid u$; in the second case we are done, and in the first, if $t \ge 1$ then $t \in S$ gives $q \mid u$, while if $t = 0$ then $u^{t} = 1$ and $q \mid 1$ is impossible for a prime, since $q > 1 > 0 > -1$ would then be contradicted. So $\sigma(t) \in S$ and $S = \mathbb{N}$. [step 1.1, L4, L9, L10, L12, L13, L14]
items/cor-rational-root-of-an-integer-is-an-integer.md-101-
