items/ex-two-continuous-real-functions-agreeing-on-the-rationals-are-equal.md:79:1.1 $\mathbb{Q}_{\mathbb{R}}$ is dense in $\mathbb{R}$: given a nonempty open $U$, pick $x \in U$ and by [A1] a real $r > 0$ with $(x-r, x+r) \subseteq U$; by [L1] some rational lies strictly between $x - r$ and $x + r$, hence in $U$. [A1, A2, L1]
