items/ex-raabe-decides-where-ratio-fails.md:76:1.1 Every $a_k = 1/\iota(k+1)^{2}$ is positive, so the ratios and the Raabe expression are defined. [given, L1]
items/ex-raabe-decides-where-ratio-fails.md-77-
items/ex-raabe-decides-where-ratio-fails.md:78:2.1 The ratios are $q_k = \dfrac{1/\iota(k+2)^{2}}{1/\iota(k+1)^{2}} = \dfrac{\iota(k+1)^{2}}{\iota(k+2)^{2}} = \left(1 - \dfrac{1}{\iota(k+2)}\right)^{2}$. [step 1.1, L1, algebra]
items/ex-raabe-decides-where-ratio-fails.md-79-
items/ex-raabe-decides-where-ratio-fails.md-80-2.2 The Raabe expression is $R_k = (k+1)\left(\dfrac{\iota(k+2)^{2}}{\iota(k+1)^{2}} - 1\right) = \dfrac{\iota(k+2)^{2} - \iota(k+1)^{2}}{\iota(k+1)} = \dfrac{2\iota(k)+3}{\iota(k)+1} = 2 + \dfrac{1}{\iota(k+1)}$. [step 1.1, L1, algebra]
