items/ex-ratio-fails-root-succeeds.md-58-
items/ex-ratio-fails-root-succeeds.md:59:**Given:** The alternating sequence $(s_k)$, the auxiliary $t_k \in \{2, 1/2\}$, the sequence $a_k = 2^{-k} t_k$, the ratios $q_k = a_{k+1}/a_k$ and the roots $r_k = a_{k+1}^{1/(k+1)}$, all as in [[fs-ratio-and-root-limits-always-agree]].
items/ex-ratio-fails-root-succeeds.md-60-
items/ex-ratio-fails-root-succeeds.md:61:[L1] For this sequence: every $a_k$ is positive, $q_k \in \{1/8, 2\}$ with both values occurring at arbitrarily large indices, $\liminf_k q_k = 1/8$, $\limsup_k q_k = 2$, and $r_k \to 1/2$, so $\liminf_k r_k = \limsup_k r_k = 1/2$ ([[fs-ratio-and-root-limits-always-agree]]).
items/ex-ratio-fails-root-succeeds.md-62-
items/ex-ratio-fails-root-succeeds.md:63:[L2] The chain $\liminf_k q_k \le \liminf_k r_k \le \limsup_k r_k \le \limsup_k q_k$ ([[thm-ratio-root-inequality]]).
items/ex-ratio-fails-root-succeeds.md-64-
items/ex-ratio-fails-root-succeeds.md:65:[L3] Limit superior and limit inferior in $\overline{\mathbb{R}}$ ([[def-limsup-liminf]], [[def-extended-reals]]).
items/ex-ratio-fails-root-succeeds.md-66-
items/ex-ratio-fails-root-succeeds.md-67-[L4] Powers: $2^{-k} = (1/2)^{k}$ and $t_k \le 2$, so $a_k \le 2 \cdot (1/2)^{k}$; and $a_k > 0$ ([[def-integer-power]], [[lem-power-laws]], [[def-rational-power]], [[lem-of-sign-rules]]).
