items/cex-rationals-in-an-interval-are-disconnected.md-43-endpoints, so it is order-convex as a subset of the ordered field $\mathbb{Q}$:
items/cex-rationals-in-an-interval-are-disconnected.md-44-it is an interval of that field. As a subset of $\mathbb{R}$ it is nevertheless
items/cex-rationals-in-an-interval-are-disconnected.md:45:disconnected, split at the irrational point $\sqrt 2$. So the equivalence of
items/cex-rationals-in-an-interval-are-disconnected.md-46-[[thm-connected-subsets-of-r-are-intervals]] genuinely uses the completeness of
items/cex-rationals-in-an-interval-are-disconnected.md-47-$\mathbb{R}$, and "is an interval of the order it carries from $\mathbb{Q}$" is
items/cex-rationals-in-an-interval-are-disconnected.md-48-not enough to make a set connected.
