items/ex-the-hat-check-ratio-as-a-quotient-of-counts.md-94-1.2 The derangement numbers up to $6$. From $D_2 = 1$ and [L3]: $\iota(D_3) = 3\cdot 1 - 1 = 2$, $\iota(D_4) = 4\cdot 2 + 1 = 9$, $\iota(D_5) = 5\cdot 9 - 1 = 44$ and $\iota(D_6) = 6\cdot 44 + 1 = 265$; since $\iota$ is injective these are the natural numbers $D_3 = 2$, $D_4 = 9$, $D_5 = 44$, $D_6 = 265$. [L2, L3, L4]
items/ex-the-hat-check-ratio-as-a-quotient-of-counts.md-95-
items/ex-the-hat-check-ratio-as-a-quotient-of-counts.md:96:2.1 The tabulated ratios. Dividing the base values in [L3] and the values from step 1.2 by the factorials of [L5] gives $r_0 = 1/1 = 1$, $r_1 = 0/1 = 0$, $r_2 = 1/2$, $r_3 = 2/6 = 1/3$, $r_4 = 9/24 = 3/8$, $r_5 = 44/120 = 11/30$ and $r_6 = 265/720 = 53/144$. [step 1.2, L3, L4, L5]
items/ex-the-hat-check-ratio-as-a-quotient-of-counts.md-97-
items/ex-the-hat-check-ratio-as-a-quotient-of-counts.md-98-2.2 A cross-check at $n = 4$ through step 1.1: $\sum_{i<5}(-1)^{i}/\iota(i!) = 1 - 1 + 1/2 - 1/6 + 1/24 = 9/24 = 3/8$, which is $r_4$. [step 1.1, L4, L5]
