items/cex-ratio-inconclusive-root-decides.md-60-
items/cex-ratio-inconclusive-root-decides.md:61:**Given:** The alternating sequence $(s_k)$ of [[lem-alternating-sequence]]; $t_k := 2$ when $s_k = 1$ and $t_k := 1/2$ when $s_k = -1$; $a_k := 2^{-k} t_k$; and the families $q_k = |a_{k+1}/a_k|$, $\rho_k = |a_{k+1}|^{1/(k+1)}$ ([[def-limsup-liminf]], [[def-rational-power]]).
items/cex-ratio-inconclusive-root-decides.md-62-
items/cex-ratio-inconclusive-root-decides.md-63-[L1] The alternating sequence satisfies $|s_k| = 1$ for every $k$, so each $s_k$ is $1$ or $-1$ and $t_k$ is well defined with $t_k > 0$ ([[lem-alternating-sequence]], [[lem-of-abs-value]]).
items/cex-ratio-inconclusive-root-decides.md-64-
items/cex-ratio-inconclusive-root-decides.md-65-[L2] $2^{-k} > 0$ for every $k \in \mathbb{N}$ ([[def-integer-power]], [[lem-power-monotone]], [[lem-power-laws]]).
items/cex-ratio-inconclusive-root-decides.md-66-
items/cex-ratio-inconclusive-root-decides.md:67:[L3] For this sequence, $\liminf_k q_k = 1/8$, $\limsup_k q_k = 2$ and the root family converges to $1/2$, so $\limsup_k \rho_k = 1/2$ ([[fs-ratio-and-root-limits-always-agree]]).
items/cex-ratio-inconclusive-root-decides.md-68-
items/cex-ratio-inconclusive-root-decides.md:69:[L4] The root test: $\limsup_k \rho_k < 1$ gives convergence of $\sum_{k \ge 1} |a_k|$ ([[thm-root-test]]).
items/cex-ratio-inconclusive-root-decides.md-70-
items/cex-ratio-inconclusive-root-decides.md:71:[L5] The ratio test: its convergence half needs $\limsup_k q_k < 1$ and its divergence half needs $\liminf_k q_k > 1$; those are its only two criteria ([[thm-ratio-test]]).
items/cex-ratio-inconclusive-root-decides.md-72-
items/cex-ratio-inconclusive-root-decides.md:73:[L6] Limit superior and inferior exist in $\overline{\mathbb{R}}$ for every sequence ([[lem-limsup-exists]], [[def-limsup-liminf]]); a series converges if and only if each of its tail series converges ([[lem-series-tail-invariance]], [[def-series]]).
