items/fs-sqrt2-rational.md-35-
items/fs-sqrt2-rational.md-36-**Given:** The rationals as quotients of integer pairs ([[def-rationals]]).
items/fs-sqrt2-rational.md-37-
items/fs-sqrt2-rational.md:38:[A1] Every rational can be written $a/b$ in lowest terms, with $a, b$ not both even (cancel common factors of $2$; the process terminates by well-ordering of $\mathbb{N}$).
items/fs-sqrt2-rational.md-39-
items/fs-sqrt2-rational.md-40-[A2] Parity in $\mathbb{Z}$: if $k^2$ is even then $k$ is even (an odd $k = 2j+1$ has odd square $4j^2 + 4j + 1$).
items/fs-sqrt2-rational.md-41-
--
items/fs-sqrt2-rational.md-51-
items/fs-sqrt2-rational.md-52-4.1 Substituting: $4c^2 = 2b^2$, so $b^2 = 2c^2$ is even, hence $b$ is even. [step 3.1, A2, algebra]
items/fs-sqrt2-rational.md-53-
items/fs-sqrt2-rational.md:54:5.1 Both $a$ and $b$ are even, contradicting the lowest-terms choice of step 1.1; the assumption fails: no rational squares to $2$. [step 4.1, step 1.1, discharge-contradiction] ∎
