items/ex-strict-ratio-root-chain.md-66-
items/ex-strict-ratio-root-chain.md:67:**Given:** The alternating sequence $(s_k)$ with index maps $e, o$ ([[lem-alternating-sequence]]); the sequence $a_k$ defined above; the ratios $q_k = a_{k+1}/a_k$; and the roots $r_k = a_{k+1}^{1/(k+1)}$.
items/ex-strict-ratio-root-chain.md-68-
items/ex-strict-ratio-root-chain.md-69-[L1] The alternating sequence: $|s_k| = 1$, $s_{k+1} = -s_k$, $s_{e_j} = 1$, $s_{o_j} = -1$, with $e$, $o$ strictly increasing, so $e_j \ge j$ and $o_j \ge j$; also $o_0 = \sigma(0) \ge 1$ ([[lem-alternating-sequence]], [[lem-index-map-grows]]).
items/ex-strict-ratio-root-chain.md-70-
items/ex-strict-ratio-root-chain.md:71:[L2] Limit superior and limit inferior in $\overline{\mathbb{R}}$: existence for every sequence, the tail supremum being the least upper bound of the tail range and the tail infimum its greatest lower bound ([[def-limsup-liminf]], [[lem-limsup-exists]], [[lem-extended-reals-complete]], [[def-upper-bound]], [[def-partial-order]], [[def-sequence]]).
items/ex-strict-ratio-root-chain.md-72-
items/ex-strict-ratio-root-chain.md-73-[L3] The order on $\overline{\mathbb{R}}$ is total, $+\infty$ is greatest, every real is $< +\infty$, and the order restricts on $\mathbb{R}$ to the order of $\mathbb{R}$ ([[def-extended-reals]]).
items/ex-strict-ratio-root-chain.md-74-
