items/ex-strict-ratio-root-chain.md-81-[L7] The order on $\mathbb{N}$ is total, so any two indices have a common upper bound ([[def-nat-order]], [[thm-nat-linear-order]]).
items/ex-strict-ratio-root-chain.md-82-
items/ex-strict-ratio-root-chain.md:83:[L8] The chain $\liminf_k q_k \le \liminf_k r_k \le \limsup_k r_k \le \limsup_k q_k$ ([[thm-ratio-root-inequality]]).
