items/ex-sup-rationals-below-sqrt-two.md-54-
items/ex-sup-rationals-below-sqrt-two.md-55-This is the reason $\mathbb{R}$ exists. The rationals form an ordered field in
items/ex-sup-rationals-below-sqrt-two.md-56-which a perfectly ordinary bounded set fails to have a least upper bound, because
items/ex-sup-rationals-below-sqrt-two.md:57:the number that ought to be that bound is irrational ([[fs-sqrt2-rational]]). The
items/ex-sup-rationals-below-sqrt-two.md-58-least-upper-bound property ([[def-complete-ordered-field]]) is precisely the
items/ex-sup-rationals-below-sqrt-two.md-59-repair, and the value it supplies here is $\sqrt{2}$.
