items/ex-lipschitz-extension-from-the-rationals.md-80-
items/ex-lipschitz-extension-from-the-rationals.md-81-1.1 By [A1] and [L1] the map $f$ is uniformly continuous on the subspace $\mathbb{Q}$ of $\mathbb{R}$. [A1, L1]
items/ex-lipschitz-extension-from-the-rationals.md-82-
items/ex-lipschitz-extension-from-the-rationals.md:83:1.2 Let $x,y \in \mathbb{R}$. By density and [L5] there are sequences $(p_k)$ and $(q_k)$ of rationals with $p_k \to x$ and $q_k \to y$. [L2, L5]
items/ex-lipschitz-extension-from-the-rationals.md-84-
items/ex-lipschitz-extension-from-the-rationals.md:85:2.1 $\mathbb{Q}$ is dense in $\mathbb{R}$ and $\mathbb{R}$ is complete, so [L4] supplies a uniformly continuous $F : \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ with $F(q) = f(q)$ for every rational $q$, and $F$ is the only continuous map $\mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ with that property. [step 1.1, L2, L3, L4]
items/ex-lipschitz-extension-from-the-rationals.md-86-
items/ex-lipschitz-extension-from-the-rationals.md-87-2.2 Likewise $p_k - q_k \to x - y$, so $|p_k - q_k| \to |x-y|$ and $L\,|p_k - q_k| \to L\,|x-y|$. [step 1.2, L7, L8]
items/ex-lipschitz-extension-from-the-rationals.md-88-
items/ex-lipschitz-extension-from-the-rationals.md-89-3.1 $F$ is continuous, being uniformly continuous, so $F(p_k) \to F(x)$ and $F(q_k) \to F(y)$; hence $F(p_k) - F(q_k) \to F(x) - F(y)$ and, by [L8], $|F(p_k) - F(q_k)| \to |F(x) - F(y)|$. [step 2.1, step 1.2, L6, L7, L8]
items/ex-lipschitz-extension-from-the-rationals.md-90-
items/ex-lipschitz-extension-from-the-rationals.md:91:3.2 For every $k$ the terms $p_k, q_k$ are rational and $F$ agrees with $f$ on them, so $|F(p_k) - F(q_k)| = |f(p_k) - f(q_k)| \le L\,|p_k - q_k|$ by [A1]. [step 2.1, step 1.2, A1]
items/ex-lipschitz-extension-from-the-rationals.md-92-
items/ex-lipschitz-extension-from-the-rationals.md-93-4.1 Passing to the limit in step 3.2, using steps 3.1 and 2.2, gives $|F(x) - F(y)| \le L\,|x-y|$; as $x,y$ were arbitrary reals, $F$ is Lipschitz with constant $L$. [step 3.1, step 2.2, step 3.2, L7]
items/ex-lipschitz-extension-from-the-rationals.md-94-
