items/fs-ratio-and-root-limits-always-agree.md-64-[L1] The alternating sequence: $s_0 = 1$, $s_{k+1} = -s_k$, $|s_k| = 1$ for every $k$, $s_{e_j} = 1$ and $s_{o_j} = -1$, and $e$, $o$ are strictly increasing ([[lem-alternating-sequence]]); a strictly increasing index map satisfies $n_j \ge j$ ([[lem-index-map-grows]]).
